      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRAVE XENA (1) smart mare who finds the right race second up after she caught the eye on resumption with a narrow third over 1000m at Randwick in Highway company. Goes equally as well second up and the fast tempo suits. Hard to stop. THE BIV (4) tough win first up from the rails draw, then worked hard from a wide barrier to hold a forward position before her condition gave out when sixth over this track and trip. Worth another chance at the good each-way odds. DIETRICH (2) consistent mare who was in need of the run first up when she drifted back further than anticipated with a below-par sixth over 1000m at Gosford. Regular apprentice hops back on and can bounce back from the low draw. HELLABELLA (3) used up early from the sticky gate on resumption and had nothing left in the tank when a tiring last over 1100m at Canterbury in BM72 company. Finds a weaker race from the right barrier.",
